# Hand-authored fixture data. Formatting it would produce a large, meaningless
# diff and make referential-integrity review harder; scripts/check-sample-data.mjs
# is what actually guards these files.
sample-data/

# CLAUDE.md and docs/ are the alignment layer — hand-wrapped, and read by humans
# and agents rather than compiled. Prettier's markdown handling adds churn to
# those files without making them clearer, so prose stays hand-maintained.
*.md

# Agent settings are deliberately not agent-writable, so a gate that demands a
# change here is one the agent structurally cannot satisfy — it would fail the
# pre-commit hook with no way to fix itself. Don't gate on files the thing being
# gated can't edit.
.claude/
